Clean your appliance and its parts after each use. Failure to follow these cleaning instructions may result in catastrophic failure, which may lead to property damage, severe personal injury and/or death.  Always unplug your cooker and let it cool to room temperature before cleaning. Never use metal scouring pads, abrasive powders or harsh chemical detergents on any of the pot's parts or accessories.  Let all surfaces dry thoroughly before use, and before storage.

<PIC:Manual30_29>
{{image description: Care, cleaning, and storage table listing accessories, pressure cooking lid parts, air fryer lid, cooker base, and power cord with dishwasher-safe notes and warnings not to immerse some parts.}}

Grip the edge of the silicone and pull the sealing ring out from behind the circular stainless-steel sealing ring rack.  With the sealing ring removed, inspect the steel rack to make sure it is secured centered, and an even height all the way around the lid. Do not attempt to repair a deformed sealing ring rack.  The sealing ring is easiest to remove and install when it is wet and soapy.

<PIC:Manual30_30>
{{image description: Sealing ring removal drawing showing hands pulling the sealing ring away from the underside of the pressure lid.}}

Pull the steam release valve up and off the steam release pipe.The steam release valve must be installed before using the cooker.

<PIC:Manual30_32>
{{image description: Steam release valve removal drawing with a hand lifting the valve cap upward from the top of the lid.}}

Place the steam release valve on the steam release pipe and press down firmly.  The steam release valve sits loosely on the steam release pipe when installed properly but should remain in place when the lid is turned over.

<PIC:Manual30_33>
{{image description: Steam release valve installation drawing with a hand pressing the valve cap downward onto the lid post.}}

Grip the lid like a steering wheel and use your thumbs to press firmly against the side of the anti-block shield (pressing towards the side of the lid and up) until it pops off the prongs underneath.

<PIC:Manual30_34>
{{image description: Anti-block shield removal drawing showing both thumbs pressing around the shield on the underside of the lid.}}

Place one finger on the flat top of float valve, then turn the lid over. Detach the silicone cap from the bottom side of the float valve.  Remove the float valve from the top of the lid. Do not discard the float valve or silicone cap.

<PIC:Manual30_36>
{{image description: Top view of a hand pressing a button or quick release control on the pressure cooker lid; the word Top appears below.}}

Align the grooves on the condensation collector over the tabs on the back of the cooker base and slide the condensation collector into place.

